From c58ec718c9d88e2df1d186a6f334b682f39bcfe7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: adorfer <adorferen@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 19:53:14 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 5/5] uboot-mediatek: Zyxel WX5600-T0: adapt to U-Boot 2024.10

The board patch was written for a newer U-Boot. In 2024.10 the mt7986
pinctrl node is labelled pinctrl and the GPIO controller gpio, not pio, and
several environment options still carry their old names. Without the renames
the default environment (bootmenu, bootcmd) and the redundant UBI environment
are silently dropped.

- &pio <n> -> &gpio <n>, &pio { -> &pinctrl {
- ENV_REDUNDANT -> SYS_REDUNDAND_ENVIRONMENT
- ENV_RELOC_GD_ENV_ADDR -> SYS_RELOC_GD_ENV_ADDR
- ENV_USE_DEFAULT_ENV_TEXT_FILE -> USE_DEFAULT_ENV_FILE
- ENV_DEFAULT_ENV_TEXT_FILE -> DEFAULT_ENV_FILE
- drop LED_ACTIVITY and LED_BOOT (not in 2024.10, LED blinking only)

Same option names as the Zyxel EX5601-T0 board in 24.10. Built; every option
of the defconfig ends up in .config.

Signed-off-by: adorfer <adorferen@gmail.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 .../patches/471-add-zyzel-wx5600-t0.patch     | 32 +++++++++----------
 1 file changed, 15 insertions(+), 17 deletions(-)

diff --git a/package/boot/uboot-mediatek/patches/471-add-zyzel-wx5600-t0.patch b/package/boot/uboot-mediatek/patches/471-add-zyzel-wx5600-t0.patch
